{"author":{"id":"f21006d1826991d76b358f177209294474e8c2701fc659ff8fe8b8f40ee77f55"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1748281443,"nonce":"3fLybOuqEu+PGWGHQKsaZLYfcQQ=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOCGKeh86teFMJ","github-url":"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/issues/1139#issuecomment-2910343945"},"message":"@csabaxyz i remembered that there was an option introduced to `ssh` to add a key to the agent after the first authentication years ago...\n\n```\nHost *\n  AddKeysToAgent yes\n```\n\n```\n➜ man ssh_config | rg AddKeysToAgent -A5\n       AddKeysToAgent\n              Specifies whether keys should be automatically added to a running ssh-agent(1).  If this option is set to yes and a key is loaded from a file, the key and its passphrase are added to the agent with the  default\n              lifetime,  as if by ssh-add(1).  If this option is set to ask, ssh(1) will require confirmation using the SSH_ASKPASS program before adding a key (see ssh-add(1) for details).  If this option is set to confirm,\n              each use of the key must be confirmed, as if the -c option was specified to ssh-add(1).  If this option is set to no, no keys are added to the agent.  Alternately, this option may be specified as a time  inter‐\n              val  using the format described in the TIME FORMATS section of sshd_config(5) to specify the key's lifetime in ssh-agent(1), after which it will automatically be removed.  The argument must be no (the default),\n              yes, confirm (optionally followed by a time interval), ask or a time interval.\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1748281753,"nonce":"NF/35rijLMyVFQR6YHHrX5M0+oc=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOCGKeh86teHAT","github-url":"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/issues/1139#issuecomment-2910351379"},"message":"@MartyLake i'm at a bit of a loss without a machine to reproduce your issue. assuming that there isn't custom ssh or git configuration you rely on, on your windows machine, then there isn't an existing issue i'm aware of that would lead to your `Error: repository not found` issue.\n\nYou can _try_ using a fully qualified SSH URI for the remote (`ssh://git@github.com/MartyLake/test_git_bug.git`), but I don't think this is necessarily going to solve your issue.","files":null}]}